  "metadata": {
    "title": "Central Limit Theorem: Means Turn Bell-Shaped",
    "subject": "Statistics",
    "objective": "Show means of a non-normal variable becoming bell-shaped as n grows.",
    "learner": "Knows histograms.",
    "misconceptions": [
      "The original data becomes normal",
      "CLT needs normal data to start"
    ],
    "expectedUnderstanding": [
      "The raw population can be non-normal and stays non-normal.",
      "The sampling distribution of the mean centers near the population mean.",
      "Its spread narrows as n grows.",
      "With larger n, the shape of the means distribution approaches a bell."
    ]
  },
